# Testing and verification

## Stance

- Tests are the default, not an optional extra. Spec first, then red, green, refactor: write the failing test that states the behaviour, make it pass, then clean up.
- Every change carries the test coverage its layer allows. A change that ships without tests says why in the change description.
- Never skip tests because a layer has no runner yet. Say the layer is untested and propose the smallest setup that unblocks it.

## Where tests live

- Beside the component in its folder: `focus/focus.test.tsx`, `focus/focus.stories.tsx`.
- Firestore rules and sync: `firestore-tests/rules.test.ts`, `firestore-tests/sync.test.ts`, with `firestore-tests/emulator.ts` wiring the emulators.

## Running them

- `bun test` is the runner. There is no vitest, jest, or testing-library dependency.
- `bun run test:firestore` boots the Firestore and Auth emulators (`firebase-tools@13`, project `demo-untangle`) and runs `firestore-tests/`. Any change to `firestore.rules` must pass this.
- No runner is configured for component tests yet. Adding one is a real change: propose it, do not assume it.

## Verify every change

- `bun run lint`: 0 errors (existing warnings may stay).
- `bunx tsc --noEmit`: the root tsconfig.
- Feature layout: `node .agents/skills/feature-based-architecture/scripts/validate.mjs`.
- Web UI changes: exercise the changed flow in the browser with `bun run web`. Reuse a running server; do not start a second one.

## Known drift

`mobile/`, `server.ts`, `routes/`, Vite, and `bun run dev` do not exist in this repo. Web and native are one Expo app: web renders `src/` through `components/web-app.tsx`, native screens live in `screens/`, and the API is `app/api/*+api.ts` with `server/gemini.ts`. Correct these references as you touch the files that carry them.
